course: dictionary
lesson: 9973
title: One word, many meanings: team
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A team is a group of people, or animals, that work or play together. You can work out which meaning fits by reading the words around it. «The team of doctors saved the child.» The doctors are a group working together, so team means a group that works together.
explain: «The home team won the match by two goals.» A sports team plays against other teams. The words match and goals are clues that team means a group of players in a game.
explain: Some clues show that team is an action, not a group. «They teamed up to build the den.» Teamed up means joined together to do something. Ask yourself: is it a group, or is it something people do? That question sorts most meanings.
explain: Team also appears in maths. «Put the 20 children into teams of 5.» Here the teams are equal groups of 5, so you can work out the number of teams by dividing 20 by 5, which gives 4.
fact: A team is a group of people who play or work together.
fact: A team can also be a group of animals pulling a cart or sled, such as a team of dogs.
fact: To team up means to join together to do something.
fact: Team can be a noun or a verb: team, teams, teamed, teaming.
fact: «In 2026 the 48 teams were split into 12 groups of 4», so each group had 4 teams.
exercise: «Stunt performers rehearse with their safety team.» What does team mean here? | *A group of people working together | To cheat in a game | A yellow card | A group of dogs pulling a sled
exercise: «They teamed up to clean the playground.» What does teamed up mean? | Counted off in ones and twos | *Joined together to do something | Ran away from the playground | Lost a game
exercise: «The 48 teams were split into 12 groups of 4.» How many teams were in each group? | 6 | 48 | 12 | *4
test: The Lionesses are a football team. What does team mean here? | To join together to do something | Equal groups of children in maths | *A group of players who play a sport together | A group of animals pulling a cart
test: Put 25 children into teams of 5. How many teams are there? | 4 | 20 | 25 | *5
exam: Which sentence uses team as a verb? | *«The friends teamed up to build a den.» | «The team of doctors saved her.» | «The team of dogs pulled the sled.» | «The team won the cup.»
